---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import { setupIndex as index, setupCitation as citation, ubiquitousLanguage } from '../lib/examples';

// PDD-04@v1: Setup lets a new agent find current judgment without a handoff.
// PDD-05@v1: Setup installs the rules, routing index, citations, reviews, and CLI check.
const tree = `your-repository/
├── AGENTS.md
├── pdd.config.json
└── docs/
    └── principles/
        ├── change-protocol.md
        └── pdd-01-ubiquitous-language.md`;
const skillInstall = `npx skills add Principle-Driven/pdd --skill pdd-principles`;
const skillPrompt = `Use $pdd-principles to classify this principle proposal.
Implement the correct result.`;
const install = `npm install --save-dev @principle-driven/cli
npx pdd check`;
const ci = `- name: Check decision system
  run: npx pdd check`;
const files = [
  { title: 'Principle template', href: '/starter/principle-template.md', type: 'Markdown' },
  { title: 'Complete principle example', href: '/starter/pdd-01-example.md', type: 'Markdown' },
  { title: 'Agent index', href: '/starter/AGENTS.md', type: 'Markdown' },
  { title: 'CLI configuration', href: '/starter/pdd.config.json', type: 'JSON' },
  { title: 'Change protocol', href: '/starter/change-protocol.md', type: 'Markdown' },
  { title: 'Portable shell checker', href: '/starter/check-principles.sh', type: 'Shell' },
];
const toc = [
  { id: 'create-the-files', text: '1. Create the files' },
  { id: 'write-one-rule', text: '2. Write one rule' },
  { id: 'principle-skill', text: 'Principle skill', depth: 3 },
  { id: 'add-the-index', text: '3. Add the index' },
  { id: 'cite-dependencies', text: '4. Cite dependencies' },
  { id: 'add-the-cli', text: '5. Add the CLI check' },
  { id: 'first-version-change', text: '6. Review a version change' },
  { id: 'starter-files', text: 'Starter files' },
];
---

<BaseLayout title="Set up your repository" description="Set up PDD with principle files, an agent index, code citations, review rules, and CLI enforcement." section="Repository setup" toc={toc} previous={{ title: 'A complete example', href: '/example' }} next={{ title: 'How PDD works', href: '/method' }}>
  <h1>Set up your repository</h1>
  <p class="doc-lead">Give the next developer or agent enough evidence to reconstruct your current judgment.</p>
  <p>Start with one to three rules that your codebase has earned. The following steps connect those rules to the code that depends on them.</p>
  <div class="callout"><p><strong>Before you start</strong>Identify one repeated correction or deliberate tradeoff. <a href="/example">The complete example</a> shows the system that these steps create.</p></div>

  <h2 id="create-the-files">1. Create the files</h2>
  <p>Keep the full rules in one directory. Put the agent index and CLI configuration at the repository root.</p>
  <CodeBlock code={tree} filename="Repository structure" />
  <p>The <a href="#starter-files">starter files</a> supply the template, index, configuration, and change protocol.</p>

  <h2 id="write-one-rule">2. Write one rule</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Copy the <a href="/starter/principle-template.md" download>principle template</a> into <code>docs/principles/</code>.</li>
    <li>Name the file with its token and title, such as <code>pdd-01-ubiquitous-language.md</code>.</li>
    <li>Choose one short, uppercase prefix for tokens.</li>
    <li>Give the rule a token and version, such as <code>{ubiquitousLanguage.v1}</code>.</li>
    <li>State the rule, benefit, costly failure, effects, exceptions, and history.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Use <a href="/starter/pdd-01-example.md" download>the complete example file</a> for structure. Adapt each rule until it is true for your codebase.</p>

  <h3 id="principle-skill">Principle skill</h3>
  <p>The portable skill compares a proposal with every current rule. It determines whether to use a rule, advance its version, or add a token.</p>
  <CodeBlock code={skillInstall} lang="shell" />
  <p>The installer detects supported coding harnesses. Use <code>--agent</code> or <code>--global</code> to select a different target.</p>
  <CodeBlock code={skillPrompt} filename="Agent prompt" />
  <p>If a harness cannot load skills, use the <a href="/starter/change-protocol.md" download>change protocol</a> directly.</p>

  <h2 id="add-the-index">3. Add the index</h2>
  <p>Each entry gives the contributor a current token, a short summary, and the path to the full rule.</p>
  <CodeBlock code={index} lang="markdown" filename="AGENTS.md" />
  <p>If a nested directory has its own agent index, add each applicable principle there.</p>

  <h2 id="cite-dependencies">4. Cite dependencies</h2>
  <p>Add a pinned token where code, tests, tools, or review decisions depend on the rule. State only the local dependency.</p>
  <CodeBlock code={citation} lang="javascript" filename="src/exports/download.js" />
  <p>The full rule remains in its principle file. A citation makes the dependent code discoverable after a meaning change.</p>
  <p>A “working as designed” review decision must cite a current token.</p>

  <h2 id="add-the-cli">5. Add the CLI check</h2>
  <p>Install the CLI as a development dependency. The repository lock file pins its version.</p>
  <CodeBlock code={install} lang="shell" />
  <p>Use <a href="/cli#configuration"><code>pdd.config.json</code></a> to configure your prefix, principle directory, agent indexes, and ignored paths.</p>
  <p>Exclude standalone examples and fixtures that use another project’s tokens. Keep actual governing citations in the scanned scope.</p>
  <p>Run the check on every pull request, including changes that only affect principles.</p>
  <CodeBlock code={ci} lang="yaml" filename="CI workflow step" />
  <p>Do not add a path filter. A principle-only change can make existing code citations stale.</p>

  <h2 id="first-version-change">6. Review a version change</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Give a new agent no previous context.</li>
    <li>Ask the agent to explain one decision from the repository evidence.</li>
    <li>Practice a meaning change on a branch.</li>
    <li>Run <code>pdd check</code> to find old citations.</li>
    <li>Review each dependency before updating its citation.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>The <a href="/example#change-the-version">complete example</a> shows the report for an old token.</p>

  <h2 id="starter-files">Starter files</h2>
  <p>Download the files that your repository needs.</p>
  <div class="download-list">
    {files.map((file) => <a class="download-link" href={file.href} download><span>{file.title}</span><span>{file.type} ↓</span></a>)}
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
